<% title = "Privacy Policy"; include partials/header %>
<section class="page-header"><h1>Privacy Policy</h1></section>
<div class="container prose">
  <p><em>Last updated: October 2026</em></p>
  
  <h2>What We Collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account info:</strong> Name, email address, and password (hashed) when you register.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment info:</strong> Processed by Stripe. We never see or store your card number. Stripe stores it under their PCI-compliant infrastructure.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> Pages viewed, login times, and IP addresses (for security and access monitoring).</li>
    <li><strong>Community posts:</strong> Messages and replies you write on the community board.</li>
  </ul>
  
  <h2>How We Use It</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide and maintain your account access</li>
    <li>To process payments and manage subscriptions</li>
    <li>To monitor account security (login events, unusual activity)</li>
    <li>To improve content based on what's most read</li>
    <li>To send transactional emails (receipts, important account notices)</li>
  </ul>
  
  <h2>What We Don't Do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not sell your data to third parties</li>
    <li>We do not use your information for advertising</li>
    <li>We do not share community posts publicly outside the Site</li>
    <li>We do not track you across other websites</li>
  </ul>
  
  <h2>Data Storage</h2>
  <p>Your data is stored on servers hosted by Hostinger in our region. Payment data is stored with Stripe (PCI Level 1 certified). We retain account data for as long as your account is active and for 90 days after deletion.</p>
  
  <h2>Your Rights</h2>
  <p>You can request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data at any time by emailing <strong>privacy@kindwell.org</strong>. We respond within 30 days.</p>
  
  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use a single session cookie to keep you logged in. No tracking cookies, no analytics third parties, no ad networks.</p>
</div>
<% include partials/footer %>
